# Milestone: v0.10.11-channel-and-isA
# Covers: exception regressions: uninitialized var += in catch; asString exception
#         in asTopLevelPrintable; 1:1 non-tag colon error; scheduler stuck on
#         concurrent throw + freeze scenario.
# blocked: Exception structured-throw wiring (defer-v1.x)
# matrix-row: exceptions-try-catch
#
# Reason:
#   isA() shipped at v0.10.11.  tag.freeze() shipped at v0.10.9 (D1).
#   Remaining block is Exception structured-throw wiring (defer-v1.x):
#   `catch(var e if e.isA(Float))` requires typed Exception instances;
#   the runtime currently throws diagnostic strings, not allocating
#   Exception proto instances.  The `class X { function asString() { 0/0 } }`
#   pattern and the scheduler-stuck regression case (concurrent throw +
#   freeze) depend on structured-throw plumbing connecting OP_THROW to
#   allocate-and-populate an Exception proto.  Both deferred to v1.x.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate when Exception structured-throw lands):
# # var test; try { test += 3 } catch { test = 1; test += 3 };
# # [00000001] 4
# # echo(test); [00000002] *** 4
# # ... (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/exceptions/regressions.chk)
